            data-track="collector_to_converter_click"
            data-from-page={pageSlug}
            data-to-page={ROUTES.trackingTop}
            data-link-position="comparisons-bottom"
          >
            Full GPS Tracker Comparison →
          </a>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Verdict -->
    <section class="content-section content-section--alt" id="verdict">
      <div class="section-inner">
        <h2>Verdict: Is the Aorkuler Worth It?</h2>

        <ReviewRating value={RATING} label="Final rating" />

        <p class="section-body">
          Yes, for the right buyer, and the right buyer is narrower than the marketing
          suggests. The Aorkuler is a well-made, genuinely subscription-free finder that
          works where cellular collars do not, and the hardware quality — the case, the
          collar clasp, the fit in the hand — is better than the price implies. Two
          people with no instructions worked out how to use it in a park and found a dog
          with it.
        </p>
        <p class="section-body">
          The reason it is four stars and not five is consistency. Inside 500 feet —
          well within what this thing is for — the link dropped to last-known-position
          twice. We cannot tell you whether that was distance, the re-sync, or the GPS
          update cycle, because we did not build the test to find out. None of it stopped
          us finding the dog, and the direction arrow needs the same patience. But a
          finder you have to interpret is a slower finder, and that is friction worth
          knowing about before you buy.
        </p>

        <h3>What we did not test</h3>
        <ul class="limits-list">
          <li>
            <strong>Range.</strong> We never attempted the 3.5-mile claim and have no
            figure of our own — nothing on this page is a range result
          </li>
          <li>The IP67 rating — our unit never went in water</li>
            <li>Battery life from full to empty, on either unit</li>
          <li>The $379.99 Double Dog Kit and switching between two trackers</li>
          <li>Cold-weather performance, or use under heavy tree canopy</li>
        </ul>

        <div class="callout callout--warning">
          <p class="callout-heading">No tracker is a safety plan</p>
          <p class="callout-body">
            A tracker shortens a search. It does not replace an ID tag with a current
            phone number, a registered microchip, recall training, a secure collar and
            lead, a fence you have actually checked, or supervision. If your dog is
            already missing, start with
            <a href={ROUTES.dogRanAwaySafety}>what to do if your dog runs away</a>.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="buy-stack">
          <AffiliateOfferStack
            offers={offers}
            product={{ id: aorkuler.id, name: aorkuler.name, category: aorkuler.type }}
            pageType="collector"
            pageSlug={pageSlug}
            position="verdict"
          />
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- FAQ -->
    <section id="faq">
